LLVM `masked.scatter` with overlapping addresses is guaranteed to execute stores in vector-element order from least-significant (lowest index) to most-significant (highest index), considering only lanes enabled by the mask.

It is equivalent to:

```c
for (int i = 0; i < N; i++)
  if (mask[i])
    ptrs[i] = values[i];
```

Therefore, if multiple active lanes target the same address, the highest-index active lane’s value remains there. When a scatter is split, LLVM must chain the lower-element operation before the higher-element operation to preserve this ordering.
